     "date": "2026-08-13T00:31:43Z"
    },
    "message": "feat(theme): add Velvet — deep navy base with a vibrant velvet-red accent\n\nThe dashboard gets a fourth theme: a dark navy surface with a crimson accent\n(#e6435e) tuned to clear WCAG AA (>= 4.5:1) as text on every navy surface.\nSuccess/warning/error stay outside the red family so the crimson is\nunmistakably the brand hue and never collides with \"something is failing\".\nSurfaces step up like a velvet pile (bg -> panel -> card -> hover) and the\nshadows carry a faint crimson bloom instead of flat black for the silk read.\n\nThe theme only swaps the same semantic tokens the other themes swap, so every\nsurface picks it up with zero bespoke selectors. applyTheme() must accept\n\"velvet\" or it silently falls back to midnight — added to the whitelist.\n\nTwo guard tests: token parity with the paper theme (a missing token means a\nsurface silently falls back to midnight), and WCAG contrast of text + accent\non the navy base. Both proven to fail when the theme block is removed.\n\nVerified: 79 admin tests pass; jsdom confirms 4 switcher options, the dataset\ntheme attr, all 83 emitted classes still styled, and the canvas charts feed\nthe velvet accent. Contrast ratios measured: body 15.6:1, accent-on-navy\n4.76:1, status ok/warn/error 9.75/9.97/6.75:1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
